scsi: lpfc: Refactor calls on fc_disctmo to lpfc_set_disctmo in RSCN handler

jira KERNEL-1930
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9
commit-author Nigel Kirkland <nkirkland2304@gmail.com>
commit 75ae9d50b8430246871af493f02bfff38257ee7b
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9/75ae9d50.failed

The lpfc_set_disctmo() routine is not used for all cases when the driver
needs to restart discovery on the fc_disctmo timer.  Not doing so, makes
discovery timer actions invisible in some cases as they do not get
logged.  This patch substitutes calls on fc_disctmo to use
lpfc_set_disctmo() in lpfc_els_rcv_rscn().

	Signed-off-by: Nigel Kirkland <nkirkland2304@gmail.com>
	Tested-by: Ewan D. Milne <emilne@redhat.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261013001648.62289-7-nkirkland2304@gmail.com
	Signed-off-by: Martin K. Petersen (Oracle) <mkp@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 75ae9d50b8430246871af493f02bfff38257ee7b)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/scsi/lpfc/lpfc_els.c
diff --cc drivers/scsi/lpfc/lpfc_els.c
index cdd409c2f849,5cfe02aa27ca..000000000000
--- a/drivers/scsi/lpfc/lpfc_els.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/lpfc/lpfc_els.c
@@@ -8148,12 -8225,8 +8148,17 @@@ lpfc_els_rcv_rscn(struct lpfc_vport *vp
  			lpfc_els_rsp_acc(vport, ELS_CMD_ACC, cmdiocb,
  				ndlp, NULL);
  			/* Restart disctmo if its already running */
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +			if (test_bit(FC_DISC_TMO, &vport->fc_flag)) {
 +				tmo = ((phba->fc_ratov * 3) + 3);
 +				mod_timer(&vport->fc_disctmo,
 +					  jiffies +
 +					  msecs_to_jiffies(1000 * tmo));
 +			}
++=======
+ 			if (test_bit(FC_DISC_TMO, &vport->fc_flag))
+ 				lpfc_set_disctmo(vport);
++>>>>>>> 75ae9d50b843 (scsi: lpfc: Refactor calls on fc_disctmo to lpfc_set_disctmo in RSCN handler)
  			return 0;
  		}
  	}
@@@ -8184,11 -8257,9 +8189,17 @@@
  		set_bit(FC_RSCN_DEFERRED, &vport->fc_flag);
  
  		/* Restart disctmo if its already running */
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		if (test_bit(FC_DISC_TMO, &vport->fc_flag)) {
 +			tmo = ((phba->fc_ratov * 3) + 3);
 +			mod_timer(&vport->fc_disctmo,
 +				  jiffies + msecs_to_jiffies(1000 * tmo));
 +		}
++=======
+ 		if (test_bit(FC_DISC_TMO, &vport->fc_flag))
+ 			lpfc_set_disctmo(vport);
+ 
++>>>>>>> 75ae9d50b843 (scsi: lpfc: Refactor calls on fc_disctmo to lpfc_set_disctmo in RSCN handler)
  		if ((rscn_cnt < FC_MAX_HOLD_RSCN) &&
  		    !test_bit(FC_RSCN_DISCOVERY, &vport->fc_flag)) {
  			set_bit(FC_RSCN_MODE, &vport->fc_flag);
* Unmerged path drivers/scsi/lpfc/lpfc_els.c
